<%- | Integer $uid, Array[String] $packages, String $umask, Array[String] $suid_allowlist | -%>
AdPulse base image hardening report
Managed by Puppet (OpenVox), class adpulse::base

Controls applied:
1. Unprivileged service user: adpulse (uid/gid <%= $uid %>), shell /usr/sbin/nologin, home /opt/adpulse
2. Directories: /opt/adpulse (adpulse, 0750), /etc/adpulse (root, 0755), /var/log/adpulse (adpulse, 0750)
3. Required packages present: <%= $packages.join(', ') %>
4. Default umask in /etc/login.defs: <%= $umask %>
5. setuid/setgid bits removed from all binaries except the allow-list: <%= $suid_allowlist.empty ? { true => '(empty)', default => $suid_allowlist.join(', ') } %>
6. No world-writable files outside /tmp and /var/tmp
7. Configuration-management agent (OpenVox) and apt lists purged after apply
